message.content:
{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2146-08-24 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of the surgical team members. You're here today because of a recurring pressure sore on your sacrum. We’ve scheduled surgery later today to clean it out and close it with a flap. How are you feeling this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2146-08-24 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning, doc. I’m okay, just tired. The pain’s been worse lately, especially when I shift in the chair. Is this going to fix it for good?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2146-08-24 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re doing a V-Y advancement flap, which has a good success rate. But because you’re paraplegic and can’t move easily, pressure sores can come back. The key is using an air mattress and not putting pressure on that area after surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2146-08-24 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this done before. Last time it came back in a few months. I just don’t want to keep going through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2146-08-24 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ll do everything we can to make this one last. You’re on a good pain regimen, and we’ll keep you off the area for at least three weeks. Your plastic surgeon will follow up closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2146-08-24 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. And what about my nephrostomy? I’ve been spiking fevers again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2146-08-24 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your urine test showed signs of infection. We found Morganella morganii, which can be tricky. We wanted to change your nephrostomy tube while you’re here, but you mentioned you didn’t want that done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2146-08-24 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want them poking around with that again. Last time it hurt for days. Can’t I just take antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2146-08-24 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can treat the infection with antibiotics, and we’ve started you on cefazolin IV. But without changing the tube, the infection might not fully clear. It’s the best way to prevent future fevers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2146-08-24 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll think about it. But for now, I just want to get through the surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2146-08-24 08:18:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Understood. We’ll focus on the sacral wound today. The anesthesiologist will see you soon. Try to rest before the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2146-08-24 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mr. ___, you’re back in your room. The surgery went well. We removed the infected tissue and closed it with a flap from your buttock. You’re on a PCA pump for pain—press the button if it gets uncomfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2146-08-24 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doc. I feel groggy, but no sharp pain. Is the flap going to hold?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2146-08-24 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It looks good so far. Blood flow is strong. The next 48 hours are critical. We’ll keep you on bed rest and monitor it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2146-08-24 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the drain? I feel something pulling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2146-08-24 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a small drain to remove fluid from the site. It helps the flap heal. We’ll teach you how to empty and record the output before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2146-08-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are stable. Hemoglobin is a bit low at 8.1, but that’s expected after surgery. Your kidney function is stable—creatinine is 3.7, which we’re watching."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2146-08-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that bad? My kidneys have been off for years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2146-08-25 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s consistent with your stage 4 CKD. We’re avoiding nephrotoxic drugs. That’s why we chose cefazolin—it’s safer for your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2146-08-25 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve got enough problems without my kidneys crashing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2146-08-25 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also giving you heparin shots to prevent clots, since you’re not moving much. And we’d like you to sit up in the chair tomorrow if you can."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2146-08-25 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. But I’ve got pain in my back and shoulders from sitting so long."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2146-08-25 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can adjust your pain meds. You’re on oxycodone as needed. Let the nurse know if it’s not enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2146-08-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture came back. It’s Morganella morganii, which is sensitive to several antibiotics, including ciprofloxacin and gentamicin. But again, without changing the nephrostomy, the infection may persist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2146-08-26 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know, I know. But I don’t want the tube changed here. Can’t I just take the pills?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2146-08-26 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can switch you to oral cefadroxil, which covers this bug. But please follow up with urology soon. This isn’t something to ignore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2146-08-26 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll call them when I get home. Just get me through this recovery first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2146-08-26 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Fair enough. Your flap is looking good—warm, pink, no signs of infection. You can start advancing your diet today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2146-08-26 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’m tired of broth. Any word on when I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2146-08-26 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If all goes well, possibly tomorrow or the next day. We need to see your drain output go down and make sure you’re comfortable on oral pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2146-08-27 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your drain output is decreasing—only 25 mL yesterday. That’s a good sign. We’ll likely remove it tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2146-08-27 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’ll be a relief. Can I shower with it still in?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2146-08-27 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but keep the site clean and dry. Let the water run over it, then pat dry. Don’t submerge it. And keep the drain secured so it doesn’t pull."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2146-08-27 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I need to write down how much drains out each day, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2146-08-27 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Bring that log to your follow-up. Also, keep using the air mattress. No sitting or lying on your back for at least three weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2146-08-27 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember. Last time I didn’t, and it opened up. I’m not doing that again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2146-08-27 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Watch for redness, swelling, or darkening of the flap. If it turns blue or black, call your surgeon immediately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2146-08-27 08:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my seizures? I haven’t had one in months, but I’m on levetiracetam."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2146-08-27 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re still on your regular dose. We haven’t changed any of your home meds except for pain and antibiotics. Keep taking them as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2146-08-27 08:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my depression meds? Escitalopram and trazodone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2146-08-27 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re getting those too. We know mental health is part of recovery. If you’re feeling down or anxious, let us know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2146-08-27 08:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m okay. Just ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mr. ___, you’re cleared for discharge. Your vital signs are stable, you’re eating well, and the drain output is low. We’ll remove the drain before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Finally. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use the air mattress, keep the area clean and dry, monitor the incision, and record any drainage. Take cefadroxil twice a day for ten days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my nephrostomy? I’ll call urology, I promise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Please do. You had a positive urine culture and fevers. This infection won’t go away on its own. Follow up within a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll see plastic surgery next week?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, in seven to ten days. Call sooner if you have fever, increased pain, or flap changes. You’re going home with services—nursing will check on you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doc. I’ll take care of this one. I don’t want to be back here soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re rooting for you. Take it slow, follow the instructions, and keep in touch. You’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it. Tell the team thanks for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I will. Have a safe trip home. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—what about that lung nodule? Should I get it checked?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, as before, a follow-up CT in three months. Your primary team will coordinate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll schedule it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And keep taking your sevelamer with meals for your phosphate levels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t missed a dose. My nephrologist would kill me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Smart. Alright, I’ll sign your discharge orders. The nurse will go over everything one more time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again, doc. I mean it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in shortly to remove the drain and finalize discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—keep up with your bowel regimen. We started you on something to help prevent constipation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’ve had issues before. I’ll keep using it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2146-08-28 07:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. That’s all for now. Rest well at home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2146-08-24 00:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2146-08-28 12:09:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for a recurrent stage 4 sacral pressure ulcer and underwent successful sacral debridement with V-Y re-advancement flap coverage. He tolerated the procedure well, with stable postoperative course, adequate pain control, and gradual advancement to oral intake. He was transitioned from IV cefazolin to oral cefadroxil for antibiotic therapy. Despite fevers and a positive urine culture for Morganella morganii, he declined nephrostomy tube change during admission, though strongly advised to follow up with urology. He was discharged home with services, provided detailed wound and drain care instructions, and advised to use an air mattress and avoid pressure on the surgical site. Follow-up was arranged with plastic surgery, urology, and primary care, including imaging for a known lung nodule.",
    "problems": [
      "Pressure ulcer of sacral region, stage 4",
      "Paraplegia, unspecified",
      "Chronic kidney disease, stage 4 (severe)",
      "Neuromuscular dysfunction of bladder, unspecified",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease with stage 1 through stage 4 chronic kidney disease, or unspecified chronic kidney disease",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, not intractable, without status epilepticus",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Dorsalgia, unspecified",
      "Person injured in unspecified motor-vehicle accident, traffic, sequela",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anemia in other chronic diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Other artificial openings of urinary tract status"
    ]
  }
}
